"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"ffmpeg-devel"},"body":"1","created_at":"2026-05-21T21:23:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T21:23:51Z","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":{"id":41,"name":"new","exclusive":false,"is_archived":false,"color":"fbca04","description":"New issue/PR, needs developer review","url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/api/v1/orgs/FFmpeg/labels/41"},"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":42450,"type":"comment","html_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23197#issuecomment-42450","pull_request_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23197","issue_url":"","user":{"id":852,"login":"Forgejo_Fairy","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"forgejo_fairy@noreply.code.ffmpeg.org","avatar_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/avatars/cfaf62d2e19b313b50dd9141516d2b859344ba275ab3cb4bcf99baf76c5f7b01","html_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/Forgejo_Fairy","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2026-04-09T00:19:06Z","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"Forgejo_Fairy"},"body":"LLM review: I did a deep pass on b8cec2c36b87 over the single changed hunk plus the relevant runtime in `config_audio_output()` / `filter_frame()`.\n\nI think the patch is heading in the right direction, but I do see two blocking problems in the same sizing path:\n\n1. `av_size_mult()` is reached too late to cover all of the signed-int overflow here.\n   In `libavfilter/f_ebur128.c`, both\n   - `I400_BINS(x)  ((x) * 4 / 10)` and\n   - `I3000_BINS(x) ((x) * 3)`\n   still evaluate the multiplication in `int` before the new check runs. So `outlink-\u003esample_rate \u003e INT_MAX/4` or `\u003e INT_MAX/3` overflows before `av_size_mult()` ever sees the value. That is reachable from normal lavfi inputs: `libavfilter/asrc_anullsrc.c` accepts `sample_rate` in `1..INT_MAX`, and `libavfilter/buffersrc.c` also accepts audio `sample_rate` up to `INT_MAX`.\n\n2. The 400 ms cache can still end up with size 0 for legal inputs.\n   With `sample_rate` 1 or 2, `I400_BINS()` becomes 0. `config_audio_output()` then allocates a zero-element `i400.cache`, but `filter_frame()` immediately indexes `\u0026ebur128-\u003ei400.cache[bin_id_400 * nb_channels]`, and the wrap condition `if (ebur128-\u003ei400.cache_pos == ebur128-\u003ei400.cache_size)` can never recover once `cache_size == 0`. So this path remains unsafe for currently accepted sample rates.\n\nA straightforward way to close both holes would be to validate the window sizes before storing them in the `int` fields, e.g.:\n\n    int64_t i400_bins  = outlink-\u003esample_rate * 4LL / 10;\n    int64_t i3000_bins = outlink-\u003esample_rate * 3LL;\n\n    if (i400_bins \u003c= 0 || i400_bins \u003e INT_MAX ||\n        i3000_bins \u003c= 0 || i3000_bins \u003e INT_MAX)\n        return AVERROR(EINVAL);\n\n    ebur128-\u003ei400.cache_size  = i400_bins;\n    ebur128-\u003ei3000.cache_size = i3000_bins;\n\nand then keep the new `av_size_mult()` checks for the per-channel element counts.\n\nIf there is already some earlier sample-rate restriction that makes the above cases impossible here, please point me to it; I did not find one in the filter path I checked.","created_at":"2026-05-25T01:52:46Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T01:52:46Z","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":null,"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":42451,"type":"label","html_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23197#issuecomment-42451","pull_request_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23197","issue_url":"","user":{"id":852,"login":"Forgejo_Fairy","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"forgejo_fairy@noreply.code.ffmpeg.org","avatar_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/avatars/cfaf62d2e19b313b50dd9141516d2b859344ba275ab3cb4bcf99baf76c5f7b01","html_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/Forgejo_Fairy","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2026-04-09T00:19:06Z","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"Forgejo_Fairy"},"body":"1","created_at":"2026-05-25T01:52:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T01:52:47Z","old_project_id":0,"project_id":0,"old_milestone":null,"milestone":null,"tracked_time":null,"old_title":"","new_title":"","old_ref":"","new_ref":"","ref_issue":null,"ref_comment":null,"ref_action":"none","ref_commit_sha":"","review_id":0,"label":{"id":52,"name":"fix/bug","exclusive":false,"is_archived":false,"color":"e11d21","description":"Fixes a bug","url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/api/v1/orgs/FFmpeg/labels/52"},"assignee":null,"assignee_team":null,"removed_assignee":false,"resolve_doer":null,"dependent_issue":null},{"id":42452,"type":"label","html_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23197#issuecomment-42452","pull_request_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/23197","issue_url":"","user":{"id":852,"login":"Forgejo_Fairy","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"forgejo_fairy@noreply.code.ffmpeg.org","avatar_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/avatars/cfaf62d2e19b313b50dd9141516d2b859344ba275ab3cb4bcf99baf76c5f7b01","html_url":"https://code.ffmpeg.org/Forgejo_Fairy"